## Why This Problem Matters
This problem assesses sophisticated dynamic programming techniques by combining palindrome preprocessing, optimal substructure for non-overlapping segment selection, and explicit solution reconstruction. It integrates preprocessing with suffix-based DP while requiring careful index management.

## Key Concepts
- Palindrome table (isPal) DP preprocessing for O(1) palindrome queries
- 2D DP with optimal substructure and complete solution reconstruction
- Complexity analysis: Time O(n²k), Space O(n² + nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPalBlocks(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const isPal = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(false));

  // Precompute palindrome table
  for (let len = 1; len <= n; len++) {
    for (let l = 0; l + len <= n; l++) {
      const r = l + len - 1;
      isPal[l][r] = (s[l] === s[r] && (len <= 2 || isPal[l+1][r-1]));
    }
  }

  // Initialize DP tables
  const dp = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  const trace = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(null));

  // Fill DP table
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i + 1][t];
      trace[i][t] = {type: 'skip'};

      for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
        if (isPal[i][j]) {
          const val = (j - i + 1) + dp[j + 1][t - 1];
          if (val > dp[i][t]) {
            dp[i][t] = val;
            trace[i][t] = {type: 'take', l: i, r: j};
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let i = 0, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i < n) {
    const choice = trace[i][t];
    if (choice.type === 'take') {
      blocks.push([choice.l, choice.r]);
      i = choice.r + 1;
      t--;
    } else {
      i++;
    }
  }

  return {maxLength: dp[0][k], blocks};
}
```

## How It Works

Concise technical explanation of the mechanism.

## Key Points

- **DP State**: local[k], global[k] track ending vs non-ending subarrays
- **Transition**: local[k] = max(local[k]+a[i], global[k-1]+a[i]); global[k] = max(global[k], local[k])
- **Edge Handling**: cap K to n; initialize -inf; handles negative values

## Example

```javascript
function maxRevenue(A, K) {
  const n = A.length;
  if (n === 0 || K <= 0) return 0;
  K = Math.min(K, n);
  const global = new Array(K+1).fill(-Infinity);
  const local = new Array(K+1).fill(-Infinity);
  global[0] = 0;
  for (let x of A) {
    for (let k = K; k >= 1; k--) {
      local[k] = Math.max((local[k] !== -Infinity ? local[k] + x : -Infinity), global[k-1] + x);
      global[k] = Math.max(global[k], local[k]);
    }
  }
  return global[K];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests substring DP and reconstruction in a practical string-cleanup task, common in data processing pipelines at scale.

## Key Concepts
- DP on substrings: dp[i][j] captures minimal deletions for s[i..j]
- Reconstruction: recover exact deletions and resulting palindrome
- Complexity: O(n^2) time and O(n^2) space; can be optimized with path tracking

## Code Example
```javascript
function minDeletionsPalindrome(s) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let len = 2; len <= n; len++) {
    for (let i = 0; i + len - 1 < n; i++) {
      const j = i + len - 1;
      if (s[i] === s[j]) dp[i][j] = dp[i+1][j-1];
      else dp[i][j] = Math.min(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1]) + 1;
    }
  }
  return {deletions: dp[0][n-1], dp};
}
```

